  {
   "tipo": "explicacion",
   "titulo": "New roots in the past",
   "texto": [
    "**dar** → **dei** (di), **dizer** → **disse** (said), **vir** → **vim** (came), **ver** → **vi** (vi), **pôr** → **pus** (put).",
    "They are not the same forms as in the present: **digo** (present) and **disse** (past) are different verbs in time."
   ]
  },
  {
   "tipo": "explicacion",
   "titulo": "The terminations",
   "texto": [
    "The endings are similar to the regular ones: **-ste** (you), **-u** (him or her), **-mos** (us), **-ram** (them).",
    "Eye: **vim** (vine) and **vieste** (came) come from **vir**, and **vi** (vi) and **viste** (vestibule) from **ver**."
   ]
